  "complex_homogeneous_growth": "For EVERY dimensionN>=1,nonzero homogeneous complexP of degreeD>=1,and ANY fixed complex polynomialQ,writeA_n=E[QP^n],k_n=ceil(Dn/2),R_n=2^k_n*(N/2)_k_n. The normalized ordinary series sum(A_n/R_n)z^n is polynomial iff entire iff A_n is eventuallyzero;otherwise its radius is finite positive. Gaussian polar integration retains ALL homogeneous marker pieces and both n parities;their radial quotients are polynomials inn. Thus the normalized series is a finite polynomial-Euler combination of compact sphere resolvents,regular including infinity. Every infinite marked tail haslimsup logabsA_n/(nlogn)=D/2,withlog0=-infinity. This extends the earlier algebraic theorem to ALL complex inputs only in the LIMSUP sense;no lower bound at each nonzero index or every nonzero subsequence is asserted.",
  "borel_trichotomy": "If the marked tail is infinite,the generalized Borel series sumA_n*z^n/(n!)^s for ANY reals has radius0 fors<D/2,finitepositive radius fors=D/2,and is entire of EXACT order1/(s-D/2) fors>D/2. Stirling,Cauchy-Hadamard and the entire coefficient-order formula prove all three cases. If the tail is finite,all these series are polynomials. In particular forD>2 the ordinary exponential moment series converges at a positive radius iff the marked tail is finite;forD2 an infinite tail has finitepositive exponential radius,andD1 gives exact entire order2. Any exact prescribed non-eventuallyzero sequence of finite factorial LIMSUP ordertau,even with transcendental coefficients,forcesD=2tau under an exactc^n target law. Homogeneity and actual compact algebraic regularity are substantive.",
